From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 04:53:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 122/225] drm: sprd: carry forward the RG Rotate free-run /
 cold-init display port

Replace the clean upstream sprd dpu/dsi drivers with the proven 6.16
versions, which compile unchanged against the 7.1 DRM core. These carry
the load-bearing device bring-up that upstream lacks:

  - free-running DPI: clear BIT_DPU_DPI_HALT_EN and DSI_MODE_CFG=0 (the
    only measured config that lights this panel; the halt handshake parks
    the lanes in stopstate -> black). See DISPLAY-KNOWN-GOOD-DSI-STATE.md.
  - cold-init: soft-reset the DPU then re-apply DPI timing/panel size,
    DDR QoS (CFG1/CFG2), and properly prepare the pipe (CLK_DISPC0) and
    dpi pixel clocks instead of relying on clk_ignore_unused.
  - prepare_prev_first + early clock-lane arm in the DSI bridge.

Upstream's only non-instrumentation changes were cosmetic refactors, so
nothing of value is lost; the diagnostic register dumps are kept for the
on-device bring-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
